course: dictionary
lesson: 15205
title: The semibreve
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A semibreve is the longest common note you will meet in music. In 4/4 time it lasts four beats. «A semibreve lasts four beats, so count one, two, three, four while you hold it.»
explain: In your music book it is drawn as an open oval with no stem. «The open oval with no stem is a semibreve.» Its length is the same as two minims or four crotchets.
explain: Note lengths follow a halving pattern, just like fractions in maths. Two minims make one semibreve, and four crotchets make one semibreve too. «Two minims last as long as one semibreve.»
fact: A semibreve is the longest common note.
fact: In 4/4 time, a semibreve lasts four beats.
fact: A semibreve is as long as two minims or four crotchets.
fact: In the USA, a semibreve is called a whole note.
fact: «One semibreve fills a whole bar of 4/4 time.»
exercise: How many beats does a semibreve last in 4/4 time? | Eight | *Four | Two | One
exercise: Which note is as long as two minims? | Crotchet | Quaver | Minim | *Semibreve
exercise: «A semibreve is drawn as an open oval with no stem.» What does a semibreve look like? | *An open oval with no stem | A wavy line | A solid black dot with a long stem | A small dot with a flag
test: In the USA, what is a semibreve called? | Quarter note | Eighth note | *Whole note | Half note
test: How many crotchets last as long as one semibreve? | *Four | Two | Eight | Three
exam: Maya holds a semibreve in 4/4 time. How long does she hold it for? | Eight beats | One beat | *Four beats | Two beats
